        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Kyoto</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">794 CE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founded</span><span class="info-stat-val">Chosen in 794 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-kanmu">Emperor Kanmu</a> as the new seat of the imperial court and laid out as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heian-kyo">Heian-kyō</a> on the model of the Tang capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changan">Chang'an</a>; the Shimogamo Shrine is believed to date from the 6th century.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">In the Yamashiro (Kyoto) Basin, ringed by hills on three sides, between the Kamo, Katsura and Uji rivers, on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/honshu">Honshu</a> in the Kansai region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heian-kyo">Heian-kyō</a>, the imperial capital from 794; the Ōnin War; the Muromachi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shogun">shogunate</a>; Hideyoshi's rebuilding of the streets; Nijō Castle; about 2,000 temples and shrines; kimono weaving; the Gion Matsuri</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Today</span><span class="info-stat-val">Kyoto is the capital of Kyoto Prefecture in the Kansai region, with about one and a half million people.</span></div>
